ompany that I  want to build so that getting up out of  bed is not as difficult every morning  you have a little more belief in  yourself yes so I was funny interesting  last week I was speaking at a conference  and I said to the people in the audience  who works for a company that has a set  of values and a mission and you know  nine every single person in that group  raised their hand maybe one entrepreneur  who was just starting to do it but then  I said keep your hands raised if you  work for a company where those values  are alive where you can feel them where  when you walk into that office in the  morning or when you're walking out at  night and I'd say two-thirds of the  people lowered their hands so what I  urge people to do is is think about ways  to get those values off the walls and  into the halls and it's not rocket  science  but it does take discipline and it does  take hard work so what does that mean if  you have a certain type of culture and a  certain voice that that you speak in you  need to think about that across all  kinds of mediums of communication from  how you send people messages to emails  to how you talk on the phone to how you  present at your All Hands meeting and  there's a woman that I talk about in the  book named Ellen Bennett who's the CEO  of a very cool startup called heavy and  Bennett  they make these funky cool aprons and  now they're in over 5,000 restaurants  and and she speaks you know she she's  she could be crass you know she can drop  the f-bomb at times but she knows who  she is and she told me a fun story where  she saw two employees emailing each  other and she said guys we don't work at  Goldman Sachs like this isn't who we are  as a company and so thinking about ways  to bring those values alive you know  another example just because it's on top  of my mind from my interview with Steph  quarry from away they use slack they had  like many companies do they have a slack  channel called team love where anybody  can go on and highlight a person who's  who's lived those values another  important way to do it and that this is  a chapter in the book called mind your  meetings many of us big companies small  companies and every company in between  we are spending more and more time in  our day in meetings so why not use that  instead of being blind and everybody  just texting under the table and and you  know just getting through the meeting  why not make sure that that meeting has  a purpose that you're using that time to  really connect with the people that you  work for and moving not only your agenda  but also your values and who you are  forward so a meet in the live chat is  asking if this applies can you apply  this to networking as well or is it only  for internal yes you can 100% apply this  to networking when I think about  meetings let's take that from a  networking perspective and you're out  there talking to people I break that  down into purpose you know what is the  purpose of this networking event should  you go should you not go I mean we all  have very limited time if you've  assessed that this is the right you know  we're paying event for you that brings  us to number two which is presence be  present we know that physical presence  and psychological and for mental  presence are two very different things  so bring your human to work bring your  human to this networking event when  you're there you know don't don't look  down at your text in the middle of  having a conversation with with with a  person it's not gonna go well and the  last are protocols which is again left  to our own devices we're all we're often  not connecting so when you go to a  networking event be intentional whether  you're an extrovert or an introvert have  your strategies figure out ways to meet  a couple of people and decide in the  beginning what your purpose is and what  you want to get out of that event a lot  of people these entrepreneurs watching  they have a sense of their mission th